# TypeScript conventions

- Match existing file style: tabs, naming, comment density.
- `import type` for type-only imports.
- `strict` is on; avoid loosening types without reason. `any` appears in attributes/messaging by design.
- Prefer explicit `Component<Props>` generics for new components.
- Public exports go through barrel `index.ts` files.
- Peer Pixi types come from `pixi.js` v8+; do not bundle a second Pixi copy into the library API.
- When editing wrappers, keep `implements GameObject` and proxy forwarding complete — missing forwards break the ECS facade.
